    summary_en: "Apple has introduced significant updates to Apple Wallet in iOS 27, with a core feature being the addition of 'Physical Pass Import' capability. This feature allows users to digitize physical passes—such as membership cards, peripheral cards, and event tickets—by scanning or photographing them directly using the iPhone camera or Apple Wallet. Previously, although Apple Wallet could replace many physical cards (such as credit cards, driver's licenses, and transit cards), users still needed to carry separate physical passes that were widely used. The iOS 27 update aims to solve this pain point by centralizing all digital passes, significantly reducing the user's burden of memory. Through this feature, users can convert physical cards into digital passes and display them as barcodes or QR Codes on the iPhone or Apple Watch. This update strengthens the integration of the Apple ecosystem, making Wallet a more comprehensive digital storage hub for daily necessities.",
