    summary_en: "This article reports on a long-circulating historical documentary from Apple concerning the 'Antennagate' incident. This event occurred after the release of the iPhone 4, when users discovered that the phone's signal strength was significantly affected by how it was held. Apple quickly held an event where Steve Jobs explained that the signal issue was not limited to a single product, and offered users the choice of a free protective case or a full refund. During this Q&A, Jobs, then COO Tim Cook, and Mac Hardware Engineering Senior VP Bob Mansfield responded to media questions. The reappearance of this historical footage allows the public to review Apple's process regarding early product design, user experience, and market crisis response. The article emphasizes the value of this historical material, urging readers to watch it quickly, as it may disappear at any time.",
