    category: "Android",
    title: "Readwise Reader for Android 存在跨站腳本攻擊漏洞，透過未經清理的元數據傳播",
    summary: "Readwise Reader 的 Android 版本因處理匯入文件元數據時缺乏 HTML 清理機制，存在跨站腳本攻擊（XSS）漏洞。攻擊者可以利用受控的元數據欄位，例如作者（author）Meta Tag，將惡意內容插入到 WebView 中。當在同步設備上開啟包含惡意文件的設備時，此儲存型 XSS 漏洞將會執行，造成安全風險。本漏洞的攻擊向量是透過惡意文件元數據，影響範圍為使用 Readwise Reader 的 Android 用戶。修補建議是開發者必須在處理和渲染匯入文件元數據時，實施嚴格的 HTML 清理和輸入驗證機制，以防止惡意腳本的執行。",
    tags: ["Readwise Reader", "Android", "XSS", "CVE-2026-18311", "HTML Sanitization"],
    title_en: "Readwise Reader for Android has Cross-Site Scripting Vulnerability via Unsanitized Metadata",
    summary_en: "The Android version of Readwise Reader contains a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability due to a lack of HTML sanitization mechanism when processing imported file metadata. An attacker can exploit controlled metadata fields, such as the author Meta Tag, to inject malicious content into the WebView. When a device containing the malicious file is opened on a synchronized device, this stored XSS vulnerability will execute, posing a security risk. The attack vector for this vulnerability is through malicious file metadata, affecting Android users who use Readwise Reader. The recommended fix is that developers must implement strict HTML sanitization and input validation mechanisms when processing and rendering imported file metadata to prevent the execution of malicious scripts.",
    tags_en: ["Readwise Reader", "Android", "XSS", "CVE-2026-18311", "HTML Sanitization"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-18311", lang: "EN" }
    ]
