    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Android",
    title: "Readwise Reader for Android 存在 SVG 內容未經淨化的 XSS 漏洞",
    summary: "Readwise Reader 應用程式的 Android 版本，因其使用 `sanitize-html` 配置，允許 SVG 和 PATH 元素上的所有屬性，導致安全風險。此配置的萬用字元屬性規則未能移除像 `onload` 或 `onerror` 這樣的事件處理器屬性。攻擊者可以提供包含惡意 SVG 內容的文件，該內容能夠繞過淨化機制，並在 Reader 的 WebView 中執行腳本，進而導致客戶端跨站腳本攻擊（XSS）。本漏洞的利用路徑為惡意文件內容，影響用戶在閱讀器中的資料安全。建議 Readwise Reader 應加強對 SVG 內容的淨化處理，特別是必須移除所有潛在的事件處理器屬性，以防止惡意腳本的執行。",
    tags: ["Readwise Reader", "Android", "SVG", "XSS", "sanitize-html", "跨站腳本攻擊"],
    title_en: "Readwise Reader for Android has XSS vulnerability due to unpurified SVG content",
    summary_en: "The Android version of the Readwise Reader application presents a security risk because its use of `sanitize-html` configuration allows all attributes on SVG and PATH elements. This configuration's universal character attribute rule fails to remove event handler attributes such as `onload` or `onerror`. An attacker can provide a file containing malicious SVG content that bypasses the sanitization mechanism, executing scripts within the Reader's WebView, thereby leading to a client-side Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attack. The exploitation path for this vulnerability is malicious file content, affecting user data security while using the reader. It is recommended that Readwise Reader strengthen its sanitization process for SVG content, specifically by removing all potential event handler attributes, to prevent the execution of malicious scripts.",
