    title_en: "EGLU Corporation Announces AI-Powered Autonomous SOC, Transforming Security Paradigms",
    summary_en: "EGLU Corporation announced that to counter increasingly advanced and complex AI-driven cyberattacks, it is redefining the standard for security operations as 'Agentic SOC.' Recent cyber threats have reached a higher level; the volume of threats has increased by approximately 5.8 times compared to 2019, and the internal propagation time has also shortened. EGLU Corporation aims to overcome the rule-based limitations of traditional SOAR solutions by proposing an autonomous workflow where multiple AI agents independently understand the contextual situation and execute responses. When an incident occurs, the system uses an LLM to determine if it is a true positive or a false positive. If it is a true positive, it automatically generates customized detection strategies for SIEM and SOAR, and executes blocking. This significantly reduces the response time from detection and analysis to report generation, shortening the average time from 30 minutes to 12 seconds. Furthermore, it integrates the Attack Surface Management (ASM) solution 'I² AXIS asm' to achieve multi-layered control over threat propagation paths. However, to manage the risks associated with AI agents, it maintains a 'Human on the loop' system, thereby revolutionizing the operational paradigm for security practitioners. These professionals are no longer required to perform repetitive tasks but are instead retrained to focus on high-level Threat Hunting Architect roles.",
